@packages/core import { SigilCore }

component SigilCompilationTarget {
  goal {
    Own compiler target variants, deterministic target resolution against one
    loaded workspace, source-position semantics, component-set expansion, and
    workspace scheduling.
  }

  interface {
    CompilationTarget {
      CompilationTarget is a tagged union of component, file, location, and workspace

      a component target contains kind component, an exact case-sensitive component
      name, and an optional normalized workspace-relative declarationPath

      a file target contains kind file and one normalized workspace-relative loaded
      Sigil filePath

      a location target contains kind location, one normalized workspace-relative
      loaded Sigil filePath, and a source position

      a workspace target contains kind workspace and no additional selector

      resolve(resolvedWorkspace, CompilationTarget) returns one or more exact loaded
      component identities in deterministic scheduling order or rejects with
      COMPILER_INVALID_INVOCATION

      name-only component selection must resolve exactly one loaded declaration;
      declarationPath, filePath, and location targets must remain inside the selected
      workspace and resolve through its loaded source selection

      source positions use one-based physical lines and one-based UTF-16 code-unit
      columns, with LF and CRLF each delimiting one physical line

      component and expand ranges are start-inclusive and end-exclusive; their
      opening and closing delimiter characters are inside the selectable range, while
      the position immediately after the closing delimiter is outside
    }
  }
}

expand SigilCompilationTarget {
  logic {
    CompilationTarget {
      Ask SigilCore to normalize and validate every target path against the supplied
      resolved workspace and its loaded source selection.

      Resolve a component target by exact case-sensitive name and optional
      declarationPath. Name-only selection requires exactly one loaded declaration; a
      supplied declarationPath must identify that exact declaration.

      Ask the SigilCore semantic model to resolve a location target's one-based
      physical line plus UTF-16 code-unit column through its start-inclusive,
      end-exclusive component and expand ranges. Do not independently parse source,
      calculate coordinates, or reconstruct declaration ranges.

      When no component or expand encloses the requested position, reject with
      COMPILER_INVALID_INVOCATION.

      Resolve a file target to every component declaration in that file and to the
      parent component identity of every expand in that file. Deduplicate the result
      by exact declaration identity.

      Resolve a workspace target to every component declaration loaded through the
      selected configured workspace's source selection. Expands add evidence for
      their parent component but do not add another scheduled component identity.

      Condense the resolved component dependency graph into strongly connected groups
      and topologically order those groups. Break ties among independent groups and
      members by normalized workspace-relative Sigil path, declaration start offset,
      then exact component name.

      Preserve SIGIL_IMPORT_CYCLE from deterministic resolution for every cyclic
      group. Mark that group unavailable for agentic evaluation while independent
      acyclic groups retain deterministic order.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    LocationBasedCompilation {
      Decision: Represent an editor selection as a file-backed source position and
      delegate resolution of its enclosing component or expand to SigilCore's
      deterministic semantic model and source ranges.

      Scope: Governs location targets across compiler, CLI, and editor compilation;
      excludes workspace and explicit file-wide targets.

      Trade-offs: The public target and CLI option contracts gain source-position
      fields.

      Design issues addressed: Name-only selection cannot distinguish duplicate
      components and textual prefix scanning cannot identify expand-only files.

      Discarded alternatives: Editor-side Sigil parsing and name-only component
      selection were rejected because they duplicate semantics or lose component
      identity.

      Consequences: A cursor resolves to one core-derived component identity without
      duplicating parsing in the editor or source-position resolution in the
      compiler.
    }

    ComponentCenteredCompilation {
      Decision: Make components the primary compilation unit and resolve file and
      workspace targets into component sets.

      Scope: Governs component, file, and workspace target membership across CLI,
      editor, and CI surfaces; excludes dependency scheduling order.

      Trade-offs: File targets may select parent components whose declarations live
      elsewhere, and workspace targets evaluate every loaded component declaration.

      Design issues addressed: Declaration-only file selection hides expand-owned
      evidence, while an undefined workspace collection makes compile-workspace
      results dependent on host interpretation.

      Consequences: A component cannot appear green while a matching expand or
      relevant relationship remains unevaluated; every host resolves the same file
      and workspace membership.
    }

    DeterministicWorkspaceScheduling {
      Decision: Schedule strongly connected dependency groups topologically and use
      normalized path, declaration offset, and exact name as deterministic
      tie-breakers.

      Scope: Governs workspace-target component scheduling; excludes stage dependency
      order and evaluator-internal inspection order.

      Trade-offs: Cyclic groups cannot receive agentic evaluation even when
      independent acyclic groups can continue.

      Design issues addressed: Dependency order alone does not order unrelated
      components and cannot topologically order a cycle.

      Discarded alternatives: Discovery order and aborting the entire workspace on
      one cycle were rejected as unstable or unnecessarily broad.

      Consequences: Repeated workspace runs schedule identical evidence identically,
      while SIGIL_IMPORT_CYCLE remains an explicit deterministic finding.
    }
  }

  cases {
    CompilationTarget {
      Compiling one component includes every matching expand even when those expands
      live in other files.

      Compiling a position inside an expand resolves the component represented by
      that expand.

      A position on the first character of a component or expand range and a position
      on its closing delimiter select it. The position immediately after the closing
      delimiter does not.

      LF and CRLF each advance one physical line. A column counts one-based UTF-16
      code units and a position on a line-ending sequence selects no delimiter text.

      A position outside every component and expand rejects with
      COMPILER_INVALID_INVOCATION.

      Independent components use normalized path, declaration offset, and exact name
      order. A cyclic dependency group produces SIGIL_IMPORT_CYCLE and is unavailable
      for agentic evaluation while independent acyclic groups continue.

      A file containing one component declaration and an expand for another component
      selects both exact identities once. An expand-only file selects its parent
      component once.

      A workspace target selects every component declaration loaded by configured
      source selection and excludes documents omitted by that selection.

      A name-only component target matching two declarations, a declarationPath that
      names a different declaration, and any excluded or outside-workspace path
      reject with COMPILER_INVALID_INVOCATION before evaluation.
    }
  }
}
